From f6723236207f05e4798f996a083169607574d3d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 13:45:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] media: platform: add the HiSTB VPSS video processing
 driver

The block sits between a decoder and an encoder or a display and has no
mainline driver. Only tone mapping, temporal noise reduction, a second
output port and a write-back capture channel have no V4L2 mem2mem shape,
so they stay unimplemented. Add the driver as a mem2mem device: the
probe path, the two queues, the register layer and the job path, the
horizontal and vertical flips, the payload and timestamp of the frame
actually written, the crop taken from the selection API and the scaler
driven by the block's own phase tables. An interlaced field is bobbed
into a frame through the pre-scaler's field filter while the capture
rectangle is twice its height, and any other interlaced combination is
refused with a warning instead of silently converting; the buffers a
stopped queue still holds come back at stop_streaming.

Beyond the flip-and-scale core the driver covers the 4:2:2 format family
on both ports, the sharpening engine, a source-side crop, rotation
through a two-image chain, packed 4:2:2 input and the block's
motion-adaptive deinterlace mode; the vpss_v4_0 generation of
hi3798mv200 runs its jobs through the chained-descriptor command path
that generation uses.

Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
